IMPORT prelude

-- Massage Establishments Act 2017 (Singapore) -- the licensing offences and who is a repeat offender (s 5), who a licensee may
-- employ and the penalty (s 13), renewal of licences and employment approvals (ss 8(3), 16(2)(b)), the Licensing Officer's power to
-- suspend (s 11) and revoke (s 12(1)) with the Schedule of specified offences, the notice period for representations (ss 10(3), (4),
-- 12(3), (4), 17(3), (4)), terminating a worker after cancellation (s 17(6)), appeals to the Minister and their deadlines (ss 7(9),
-- 10(7), 12(7), 15(6), 17(8), 22, 31), the premises closure order (ss 19, 21), and the landlord's position after a conviction
-- (ss 28(6), 29(1)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/MEA2017.txt. The cover says it "incorporates all
-- amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; the page furniture reads "Informal
-- Consolidation - version in force from 17/8/2026". Later amendments are annotated in the text, the latest being G.N. No.
-- S 557/2026 (amending the Schedule, Penal Code part; commencement 17 August 2026), the last entry in the deposited legislative
-- history. SSO's metadata calls it the "Current version as at 01 Oct 2026".
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Chosen for its everyday-life relevance to ordinary people in Singapore: it governs every massage parlour, spa and
-- reflexology shop that offers massage in the course of business, the people who work in them, and the landlords who let premises
-- to them. SCOPED to what an operator, a worker, a landlord or a member of the public meets. Not encoded: the application procedure
-- and the matters the Licensing Officer must weigh (ss 6, 7(1)-(7), 14, 15(1)-(3)) beyond the appeal route; licence conditions and
-- their modification beyond the notice period (ss 9, 10); entry, inspection and investigation powers (ss 23-26), except that they
-- exist; the offences of false statements, obstruction and breach of condition (s 27); the duty to pass on an owner's notice up the
-- chain of tenancies (s 28(1)-(5)); the closure order's duties beyond the key deadline, and its costs (s 19(2), (5), (6)); the lock
-- offence (s 20); exemption (s 32); the deeming of massage establishments as public places for the Liquor Control (Supply and
-- Consumption) Act 2015 (s 34); rules (s 35) and transitional provisions (s 36). No rules made under s 35 were retrieved, so no fee,
-- qualification or prescribed criterion is known.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text, following the conventions of the example naive rows. No pipeline, no coverage
-- table, no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Massage Establishments Act 2017 -- licensing and employment`

§§ `2 and 5 -- the licensing offences`

-- s 2(1): "massage" is "rubbing, kneading, or manipulating the human body ... for the purpose of relaxing muscle tension, stimulating
-- circulation, increasing suppleness or otherwise". s 2(2): a person carries on the business of providing massage services "if the
-- person provides massage services in the course of business, whether or not those services are accompanied by any other service or
-- supply of goods".
-- s 5(1): "A person must not carry on the business of providing massage services in an establishment for massage unless the person
-- is authorised to do so at those premises by a licence". (2): must not "advertise or otherwise hold out" without a valid licence for
-- those premises. (3): an owner or occupier must not allow premises to be used by a person "whom the owner or occupier knows" is
-- doing so unlicensed. s 32: the Minister may exempt premises by order in the Gazette.
GIVEN `provides massage in the course of business` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the massage comes with other services or goods` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `holds a licence for those premises` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the premises are exempted by Gazette order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `carrying on the business is an offence` IF
        `provides massage in the course of business`
    AND (NOT `holds a licence for those premises`)
    AND (NOT `the premises are exempted by Gazette order`)

GIVEN `advertises or holds out a massage business at the premises` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds a valid licence for those premises` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `advertising is an offence` IF
    `advertises or holds out a massage business at the premises` AND (NOT `holds a valid licence for those premises`)

GIVEN `allows the premises to be used by the operator` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the operator is unlicensed for those premises` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knows the operator is unlicensed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner or occupier commits an offence` IF
    `allows the premises to be used by the operator` AND `the operator is unlicensed for those premises` AND `knows the operator is unlicensed`

-- s 5(4): (a) "a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to both"; (b) "where the person is
-- a repeat offender", $20,000 or 5 years or both.
-- s 5(5): a repeat offender is one convicted under (4) for contravening (1) who has "at least one other earlier" conviction for
-- contravening (1) or under s 9(a) of the repealed Act; or for contravening (2) with an earlier conviction for contravening (2) or
-- under s 9(e) of the repealed Act. Subsection (3) -- the owner or occupier -- has no repeat-offender limb.
DECLARE Section5Offence IS ONE OF
    `carrying on the business unlicensed`
    `advertising unlicensed`
    `allowing premises to be used unlicensed`

DECLARE Priors HAS
    `earlier conviction for carrying on unlicensed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `earlier conviction under repealed Act s 9(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `earlier conviction for advertising unlicensed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `earlier conviction under repealed Act s 9(e)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `earlier conviction for allowing premises to be used` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Section5Offence, `the priors` IS A Priors
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a repeat offender under section 5(5)` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `carrying on the business unlicensed` THEN
            `the priors`'s `earlier conviction for carrying on unlicensed`
         OR `the priors`'s `earlier conviction under repealed Act s 9(a)`
    WHEN `advertising unlicensed` THEN
            `the priors`'s `earlier conviction for advertising unlicensed`
         OR `the priors`'s `earlier conviction under repealed Act s 9(e)`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Section5Offence, `the priors` IS A Priors
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine under section 5(4)` MEANS
    IF `is a repeat offender under section 5(5)` `the offence` `the priors` THEN 20000 ELSE 10000

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Section5Offence, `the priors` IS A Priors
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months under section 5(4)` MEANS
    IF `is a repeat offender under section 5(5)` `the offence` `the priors` THEN 60 ELSE 24

§§ `13 -- whom a licensee may employ`

-- s 13(1): a licensee "must not employ an individual to work in the establishment for massage except with the approval of the
-- Licensing Officer". (2): nor anyone (a) "whom the licensee knows or has reason to believe is likely to engage in, or abet another
-- person to engage in, the provision of sexual services"; (b) "who is below 18 years of age"; or (c) who has not undergone and passed
-- a medical health screening "if required to do so by the Licensing Officer".
-- s 13(3): "a fine not exceeding $5,000 and, in the case of a second or subsequent conviction, to a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to
-- imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to both". A first conviction carries no imprisonment.
DECLARE Worker HAS
    `approved by the Licensing Officer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `age in years` IS A NUMBER
    `licensee knows or has reason to believe is likely to provide sexual services` IS A BOOLEAN
    `medical screening required by the Licensing Officer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `passed the medical screening` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the worker` IS A Worker
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `employing the worker is an offence` IF
        (NOT `the worker`'s `approved by the Licensing Officer`)
    OR  `the worker`'s `age in years` < 18
    OR  `the worker`'s `licensee knows or has reason to believe is likely to provide sexual services`
    OR  (`the worker`'s `medical screening required by the Licensing Officer` AND (NOT `the worker`'s `passed the medical screening`))

GIVEN `earlier convictions under section 13` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine under section 13(3)` MEANS
    IF `earlier convictions under section 13` > 0 THEN 10000 ELSE 5000

GIVEN `earlier convictions under section 13` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months under section 13(3)` MEANS
    IF `earlier convictions under section 13` > 0 THEN 24 ELSE 0

§§ `8(3) and 16(2)(b) -- renewal`

-- s 8(3): "A licence is not renewable." s 16(2)(b): an employment approval "may be renewed upon its expiry".
DECLARE Permission IS ONE OF
    `a licence for an establishment`
    `an approval to employ an individual`

GIVEN `the permission` IS A Permission
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the permission is renewable` IF
    `the permission` EQUALS `an approval to employ an individual`

§§ `11, 12(1) and the Schedule -- suspension and revocation`

-- s 11(1): the Licensing Officer "may, without compensation, immediately suspend a licence if proceedings for an offence specified in
-- the Schedule have commenced and are pending against the licensee, a responsible officer of the licensee, or a person having
-- substantial interest in, or control or direction over, the business". (2): until the proceedings conclude.
-- The Schedule lists offences under ten Acts. Those below are read from it: Penal Code s 354 (outrage of modesty) and s 377BB
-- (voyeurism), Women's Charter s 148 (brothels), Prevention of Human Trafficking Act 2014 s 3, Employment of Foreign Manpower Act 1990
-- s 5(6) (no work pass). The PDF's tables are column-shifted; section numbers and descriptions are matched by order. Theft (Penal
-- Code s 379) and the Act's own s 5 offence are NOT in the Schedule.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `outrage of modesty`
    `voyeurism`
    `keeping a brothel`
    `trafficking in persons`
    `employing a foreigner without a work pass`
    `theft`
    `running an unlicensed massage establishment`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence is in the Schedule` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `theft` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `running an unlicensed massage establishment` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

DECLARE Person IS ONE OF
    `the licensee`
    `a responsible officer of the licensee`
    `a person with substantial interest in or control of the business`
    `an employee of the licensee`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is connected to the licence` IF
    NOT (`the person` EQUALS `an employee of the licensee`)

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `pending proceedings allow suspension` IF
    `the offence is in the Schedule` `the offence` AND `the person is connected to the licence` `the person`

-- s 12(1): may revoke if (a) procured by fraud or misrepresentation; (b) no longer fit and proper; (c) the licensee, a responsible
-- officer or a person with substantial interest or control "is convicted of an offence specified in the Schedule"; (d) the business
-- is likely to cause annoyance or inconvenience to the public; (e) massage "is or may be administered" by anyone without the approved
-- qualification; or (f) the business is or is likely to be carried on in contravention of any requirement of the Act.
DECLARE RevocationFacts HAS
    `licence procured by fraud or misrepresentation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `licensee no longer fit and proper` IS A BOOLEAN
    `connected person convicted of a Schedule offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `business likely to cause annoyance or inconvenience to the public` IS A BOOLEAN
    `massage may be administered by an unqualified person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `business likely to contravene a requirement of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS A RevocationFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is a ground to revoke the licence` IF
        `the facts`'s `licence procured by fraud or misrepresentation`
    OR  `the facts`'s `licensee no longer fit and proper`
    OR  `the facts`'s `connected person convicted of a Schedule offence`
    OR  `the facts`'s `business likely to cause annoyance or inconvenience to the public`
    OR  `the facts`'s `massage may be administered by an unqualified person`
    OR  `the facts`'s `business likely to contravene a requirement of the Act`

§§ `10(3), (4), 12(3), (4), 17(3), (4) -- time for representations`

-- Before modifying conditions, revoking a licence or cancelling an employment approval, the notice must give a time for written
-- representations that "must not be less than 14 days after the date of the notice", unless (a) the Licensing Officer thinks it in
-- the public interest to act "as soon as possible" or (b) the licensee (or, for s 17, the individual) "is contravening, or has
-- contravened, any requirement of the Act". s 11 suspension needs no notice: it is immediate.
GIVEN `days allowed for representations` IS A NUMBER,
      `public interest in acting as soon as possible` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `contravening or has contravened a requirement of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the time for representations is lawful` IF
        `days allowed for representations` >= 14
    OR  `public interest in acting as soon as possible`
    OR  `contravening or has contravened a requirement of the Act`

-- s 17(6): after cancellation of an approval the licensee "must, within 7 days after the date of the notification ... terminate the
-- employment of the relevant individual".
GIVEN `days after notification of cancellation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the worker was let go in time` IF
    `days after notification of cancellation` <= 7

§§ `7(9), 10(7), 12(7), 15(6), 17(8), 22 and 31 -- appeals to the Minister`

-- Refusal of a licence (s 7(9)), revocation (s 12(7)), refusal of an employment approval (s 15(6)) and its cancellation (s 17(8)):
-- appeal in writing "within 14 days after being notified", or, if the person requires the grounds within that period, "within 14
-- days after being provided with the grounds". The Licensing Officer must give grounds within 7 days of being asked (ss 7(8), 12(6),
-- 15(5), 17(7)). A direction modifying licence conditions (s 10(7)) and a premises closure order (s 22(1)): within 14 days after the
-- date of the direction or order, with no grounds route. s 31 lists exactly these six appeals. No appeal is provided against
-- suspension under s 11.
-- Takes effect despite appeal, "unless the Minister otherwise specifies": a direction (s 10(8)), a revocation (s 12(8)), a
-- cancellation (s 17(9)) and a closure order (s 22(2)). Reading "within 14 days" as including day 14 is an inference.
DECLARE Decision IS ONE OF
    `refusal of a licence`
    `revocation of a licence`
    `refusal of an employment approval`
    `cancellation of an employment approval`
    `direction to give effect to modified conditions`
    `premises closure order`
    `suspension of a licence`

GIVEN `the decision` IS A Decision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the decision can be appealed to the Minister` IF
    NOT (`the decision` EQUALS `suspension of a licence`)

GIVEN `the decision` IS A Decision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the grounds route extends the deadline` IF
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `refusal of a licence` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `revocation of a licence` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `refusal of an employment approval` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `cancellation of an employment approval` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the decision` IS A Decision,
      `days from notification to appeal` IS A NUMBER,
      `grounds required within 14 days of notification` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `days from receiving grounds to appeal` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appeal is in time` IF
        `the decision can be appealed to the Minister` `the decision`
    AND (    `days from notification to appeal` <= 14
         OR  (    `the grounds route extends the deadline` `the decision`
              AND `grounds required within 14 days of notification`
              AND `days from receiving grounds to appeal` <= 14))

§§ `19 and 21 -- premises closure order`

-- s 19(1): the Commissioner may issue an order to a person "(a) charged" with an offence for contravening s 5(1) (or, before, on or
-- after 1 March 2018, s 9(a) of the repealed Act) "and (b) whom the Commissioner has reasonable grounds to suspect is continuing to
-- provide massage services in premises specified in the order despite criminal proceedings ... being pending". A conviction is not
-- required; a charge for advertising (s 5(2)) is not enough.
-- s 19(2)(b): the key must reach the Licensing Officer "within 24 hours after those premises have been secured". s 19(4): $15,000 or
-- 3 years or both.
GIVEN `charged with carrying on unlicensed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `charged under repealed Act s 9(a)` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `reasonable grounds to suspect massage is continuing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Commissioner may issue a closure order` IF
    (`charged with carrying on unlicensed` OR `charged under repealed Act s 9(a)`) AND `reasonable grounds to suspect massage is continuing`

GIVEN `hours after securing the premises` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the key was handed over in time` IF
    `hours after securing the premises` <= 24

-- s 21(1): a person must not enter premises subject to an order in force "unless the person (a) is permitted by the Commissioner to
-- enter the premises; and (b) complies with any condition of entry". (2): $15,000 or 3 years or both.
GIVEN `the order is in force` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `permitted by the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `complies with the conditions of entry` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entering the premises is an offence` IF
    `the order is in force` AND (NOT (`permitted by the Commissioner` AND `complies with the conditions of entry`))

§§ `28(6) and 29(1) -- the landlord after a conviction`

-- s 29(1): "Upon the conviction of any person ... for an offence under section 5(4) for contravening section 5(1) or (3)", the owner
-- or occupier from whom the offender rents "must, within one month after the date of conviction, require the offender to deliver up
-- possession ... if the lease or tenancy is not earlier terminated". A conviction for advertising (s 5(2)) does not trigger it.
GIVEN `the offence` IS A Section5Offence, `the lease is already terminated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the landlord must require possession` IF
    (NOT (`the offence` EQUALS `advertising unlicensed`)) AND (NOT `the lease is already terminated`)

-- s 28(6): where (a) a s 28(1) notice was served on the owner or occupier from whom the offender directly rents, (b) the offender is
-- convicted, and (c) that owner or occupier fails to comply with s 29(1), then in a prosecution of that owner or occupier under
-- s 5(3) "it is presumed, until the contrary is proved," that they knew.
GIVEN `notice served on the direct landlord` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the tenant was convicted` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the landlord required possession within one month` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the landlord is presumed to have known` IF
    `notice served on the direct landlord` AND `the tenant was convicted` AND (NOT `the landlord required possession within one month`)
